(KEY-18 — `Change directory to "<path>".` is `chdir(2)`, and it really
 moves the process: a relative open after it resolves against the new
 directory.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox KEY-18.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   wrote a relative file after chdir
   cleaned up
)
Create a directory called "/tmp/voxfuzz-key-18".
Change directory to "/tmp/voxfuzz-key-18".
On error print "chdir failed".
open a file for writing called note at "marker.txt".
On error print "relative create failed".
Write "here" to note.
Close note.
Print "wrote a relative file after chdir".
Delete the file "marker.txt".
Change directory to "/tmp".
Remove the directory called "/tmp/voxfuzz-key-18".
Print "cleaned up".
